  "summary": "M2 review round 1 soft_fail fixed by OpenCode (Nemotron free). All five review findings are fixed and re-tested: (1) serve() keeps the hub db open until the stdio transport closes, with a serve() stream-pair test making a real talk call; (2) the agreement recipient (offered_to) is stored via a new migration and answers are guarded on it, including a 3-agent test where a third agent's accept is refused; (3) counter validates text before touching the store and does both writes in one transaction; (4) the integration test now asserts a reply moves the original to replied, refuses a forbidden answer through MCP, and asserts structuredContent, plus new unit tests for outlook, secret blocking (near-misses), rules reminder and claim conflicts; (5) agree claim reports only other agents' claims, the claimsOverlap alias and the no-op listMessagesFromAgent JOIN are removed, and the titleFromFirstMessage test moved into test/core/threads.test.ts. wb verify for task M2 passes: 87 tests, every acceptance command. The serve command itself (the `parley-mcp serve` CLI wiring in src/cli) is NOT part of M2; it is wired in M3 (src/cli) - recorded as an assumption below.",
